    "body": "fix on issue/3645-component-library · PR #4233 · pinned by component_files::a_project_with_a_component_table_and_its_assemblies_reopens_identically, component_files::a_file_without_a_table_and_a_holder_project_open_unchanged, component_files::a_reader_of_an_older_version_refuses_the_new_file, component_files::a_corrupt_row_or_link_refuses_the_file_by_name, component_sync::the_store_round_trips_and_refuses_a_bad_file_whole_by_name, component_sync::the_save_is_atomic_and_the_env_folder_comes_first, component_sync::a_sync_pulls_a_newer_library_copy_into_both_assemblies_and_undo_restores, component_sync::a_library_copy_that_differs_after_an_open_is_reported_never_applied · merges at the next cut\n\nThis is slice 1 and the PR uses `Refs #3645`. The PR is stacked on #4201. What stays open on this issue: `.camtools` with components and assemblies. That is version 8, because `main` is at version 7 already. The import must land the rows through the `ImportTools` undo unit. #3647 has the MCP tools and #3648 has the UI.",
