    "body": "fix on issue/3645-camtools-v8 · PR #4261 · pinned by camtools_v8::an_export_of_assembled_tools_is_version_8_and_imports_identically, camtools_v8::a_library_of_plain_tools_keeps_its_older_number_and_imports_as_before, camtools_v8::a_newer_version_and_an_older_file_with_components_are_refused, camtools_v8::a_bad_row_a_bad_link_or_an_unused_row_refuses_the_file_by_name, camtools_v8::undo_and_redo_of_an_import_with_components_restore_tools_and_table, camtools_v8::a_document_row_of_the_same_id_is_reused_when_the_same_and_refuses_when_different · merges at the next cut\n\nThis is slice 2. It is stacked on #4233 and must merge after #4233. The `.camtools` file is version 8 when a tool has a component stack. The import lands the rows and the tools in the one `ImportTools` undo step. The id rule: a row of the same id and the same content is reused; a row of the same id and a different content refuses the import by the id. The decision is in `docs/decisions/3645-camtools-v8.md`. Nothing of the issue text stays open after this PR. The MCP tools are #3647 and the UI is #3648.",
